WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 2.3 · Theory of Change
Long-term impact

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Impact is the long-term change you will contribute to, alongside many others.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:26.652
Impact is the longer-term change in people’s lives or environmental conditions that your work aims to contribute to. It may take years, and it depends on many actors beyond your founding team.

4
00:00:27.052 --> 00:00:27.652
A useful impact statement

5
00:00:27.652 --> 00:00:37.870
Whose lives change: Name whose lives, or which conditions, should improve. For example: Young people in our neighbourhood who left school early build skills and a working life.

6
00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:49.200
Narrow enough: Specific enough to guide early decisions, without claiming the whole future as yours. For example: First jobs for young people in our neighbourhood, rather than “ending youth unemployment”.

7
00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:59.878
Others involved: The other actors who already influence the same change. For example: The youth centre, local employers, the public job service and evening classes.

8
00:01:00.278 --> 00:01:00.878
Why it matters

9
00:01:00.878 --> 00:01:05.441
1. It links your everyday work to your vision.

10
00:01:05.441 --> 00:01:10.374
2. It keeps early decisions pointed at the same change.

11
00:01:10.374 --> 00:01:16.307
3. Funders and partners trust founders who name others’ part.

12
00:01:16.707 --> 00:01:17.307
How you will use it

13
00:01:17.307 --> 00:01:22.241
1. As the top of each Theory of Change pathway.

14
00:01:22.241 --> 00:01:27.544
2. To work backwards to the outcomes that lead to it.

15
00:01:27.544 --> 00:01:33.478
3. To explain your idea honestly to partners and funders.

16
00:01:33.878 --> 00:01:34.478
What to avoid

17
00:01:34.478 --> 00:01:39.041
Claiming an improvement proves your work caused it.

18
00:01:39.041 --> 00:01:43.604
A statement so broad it guides no decision.

19
00:01:43.604 --> 00:01:49.167
Forgetting the others who shape the same change.

20
00:01:49.767 --> 00:01:51.567
You write your impact statement and the other actors involved.

21
00:01:51.567 --> 00:01:55.567
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:01:57.067 --> 00:02:00.167
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
